/-!
# Round six, compact controls (I2C): the top selected bit and the record-step calculus

* `Tl_xor`: the ideal toggle is `y ⊕ (x ∧ selM n)`; with the top bit `q = ρ + n K` flipped as
  well (`flipS q`) the composite step is the slot row addition `phi g (Fpp K ρ (n+1) px py)`
  (`tlflip_phi`).
* `flip_pull`, `swflip`: the last-bit table rotation (directly when `X` is above `Y`, between two
  swaps of single bits otherwise) is the record pull `l.stepP (flipS q)`.
* `RecStep`: a program acting on the record array `flR recs M` as `recs ∘ π`, with sequencing,
  branching and skip.
* `CEnv`: the registers of the compact program; `topC_step`: the top-bit code as a `RecStep`.
-/

